opensnitch-dev: development build with inbound port scan detection
==================================================================

This package installs beside the official "opensnitch" and
"python3-opensnitch-ui" packages without sharing any file with them:

  daemon         /usr/bin/opensnitchd-dev
  configuration  /etc/opensnitchd-dev/        (PortScan enabled, policy "ask")
  eBPF modules   /usr/lib/opensnitchd-dev/ebpf/
  service        opensnitch-dev.service
  log            /var/log/opensnitchd-dev.log
  GUI            opensnitch-ui-dev, settings in ~/.config/opensnitch-dev/
  GUI socket     unix:///tmp/osui-dev.sock

The service is neither enabled nor started on install. The two daemons drive
the same nftables tables and netfilter queue, so opensnitch-dev.service
declares Conflicts=opensnitch.service: starting one stops the other. To use
this build:

  sudo systemctl disable --now opensnitch.service
  sudo systemctl enable --now opensnitch-dev.service
  opensnitch-ui-dev &

To go back:

  sudo systemctl disable --now opensnitch-dev.service
  sudo systemctl enable --now opensnitch.service

Purging opensnitch-dev keeps /etc/opensnitchd-dev/rules when it holds rules
you created: they are your data. Remove the directory by hand to forget them.

Port scan detection settings are in the "PortScan" section of
/etc/opensnitchd-dev/default-config.json; see the project wiki pages
"Port Scan Detection".
